# System Architecture & Topology

The **Galvanic Vestibular Stimulation (GVS)** system is designed to deliver controlled, bidirectional DC microcurrent through electrodes positioned over the mastoid regions behind the ears.

The system is built around an **ESP32 controller**, a **3S LiPo power source**, and a **discrete BJT H-bridge** capable of reversing the direction of current through the load.

> **⚠️ Safety Note:** This architecture is a prototype intended for controlled experimental development. Any system that applies electrical current to the human body requires appropriate electrical isolation, current limiting, fault detection, electrode/contact monitoring, and validation before human use.

---

## 1. System Components

| Component           | Description                                                    |
| ------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Controller**      | ESP32 with 3.3 V logic, dual onboard 8-bit DACs and 12-bit ADC |
| **Power Supply**    | 11.1 V nominal 3S LiPo battery                                 |
| **High-Side Stage** | Two PNP BJTs (`Q1`, `Q2`)                                      |
| **Low-Side Stage**  | Two NPN BJTs (`Q3`, `Q4`) configured as current sinks          |
| **Level Shifting**  | Two NPN BJTs (`Q5`, `Q6`) for driving the high-side PNP bases  |
| **Current Sense**   | Shared 1 kΩ emitter/sense resistor                             |
| **ADC Feedback**    | ESP32 GPIO 34                                                  |
| **Control DACs**    | GPIO 25 and GPIO 26                                            |

