# 6. Closed-Loop Current Sensing

A shared `1 kΩ` sense resistor (`Re`) is used to monitor the current flowing through the active low-side sink.

The voltage across `Re` is measured by the ESP32 ADC on:

```text
GPIO 34 → ADC → SENSE
```

Because:

```text
Re = 1000 Ω
```

the current can be estimated from the measured sense voltage:

```text
I = V_sense / Re
```

When voltage is expressed in millivolts:

```text
I (mA) = V_sense (mV) / 1000
```

### Example

If the ADC measures:

```text
V_sense = 1.5 V
        = 1500 mV
```

then:

```text
I = 1500 / 1000
  = 1.5 mA
```

The firmware periodically samples this voltage using the ESP32 ADC and uses it as a diagnostic measurement of the actual sink current.

