# 7. Operating Modes & Current Flow

The bridge provides three primary operating states.

| Mode        | High-Side | Active Sink | Current Path                                            | Polarity        |
| ----------- | --------- | ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------- | --------------- |
| **LEFT**    | `Q1` ON   | `Q4`        | `+11.1 V → Q1 → Node A → Load → Node B → Q4 → Re → GND` | Node A → Node B |
| **RIGHT**   | `Q2` ON   | `Q3`        | `+11.1 V → Q2 → Node B → Load → Node A → Q3 → Re → GND` | Node B → Node A |
| **NEUTRAL** | OFF       | OFF         | No active supply path                                   | 0 mA            |

### LEFT Mode

```text
+11.1 V
   │
  Q1
   │
   ▼
Node A (+)
   │
   │
 [ LOAD ]
   │
   ▼
Node B (-)
   │
  Q4
   │
  Re
   │
  GND
```

Current flows from **Node A → Node B**.

### RIGHT Mode

```text
+11.1 V
   │
  Q2
   │
   ▼
Node B (+)
   │
   │
 [ LOAD ]
   │
   ▼
Node A (-)
   │
  Q3
   │
  Re
   │
  GND
```

Current flows from **Node B → Node A**.

### NEUTRAL Mode

All bridge drive signals are disabled:

```text
Q1 = OFF
Q2 = OFF
Q3 = OFF
Q4 = OFF
```

The intended load current is:

```text
I ≈ 0 mA
```

